The '''Mausoleum''' is the alternative floor to the {{s|Depths}} and was added in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance]]''.

Mausoleum is an occult-themed stage full of magic and cult material. Unique features of this stage include [[Teleporters]] and {{e|Grudge}}s.

The door to the Mausoleum / Gehenna will appear after defeating the boss in The {{S|Mines}} II / {{S|Ashpit}} II or the {{S|Depths}} I / {{S|Necropolis}} I / {{S| Dank Depths}} I. The door will '''not''' spawn after defeating {{e|Mom}}. It costs two full hearts to enter, and ignores almost every form of damage reduction, including {{I|The Wafer}} and invincibility. Unlike other methods of health donation, red hearts will not be prioritized over more valuable hearts.

* {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Tainted Lost}}, {{c|Tainted Jacob}} (In his soul form), {{C|Tainted Soul}} (unless he is holding {{C|Tainted Forgotten}}), and any character under the effect of {{p|Soul of the Lost}} can enter the door for free.
* {{I|Dad's Key}}, {{p|Get out of Jail Free Card}}, {{I|Mr. ME!}}, and {{I|Sharp Key}} can be used to open the door without taking damage.
* {{t|Broken Padlock}} can be used to open the door with one bomb.
* {{i|Cracked Orb}}'s effect can open the door with less damage taken than needed, or with no damage with {{i|Dull Razor}}.
* The extra characters spawned by {{I|Strawman}}, {{P|Soul of the Forgotten}}, and {{P|Soul of Jacob and Esau}} can expend their health to open the door.
* {{t|Crow Heart}} can be used to open the door with red hearts first.

The boss of Mausoleum II is always a more powerful version of {{e|Mom}}. After Mom is defeated, a trapdoor that leads to the {{S|Womb}} II, and a sealed fleshy door both appear. Stabbing the door with the knife familiar created by {{i|Knife Piece 1}} and {{i|Knife Piece 2}} will cause it to open, leading to a more difficult version of {{e|Mom's Heart}}. Defeating Mom's Heart will cause the boss room to darken, and the trapdoor to Womb II will now lead to the {{s|Corpse}}.

* A {{i|Sharp Key}} can be used in place of the Knife.
* {{i|Cracked Orb}}'s effect can open the flesh door, allowing Isaac to keep the knife.
* If Isaac exits the {{R|Boss Rush}} room after 25 minutes have passed, there is a chance that the flesh door will change positions to the wall where the boss rush door was, causing Isaac to "come out" of the flesh door and leaving it open, allowing entry without the knife.
* After this special version of Mom's Heart is defeated, any [[Item]] or [[Pickup]] that was left behind anywhere on the floor will disappear (including {{R|Shop}} items, {{R|Angel Room}}/{{R|Devil Room}} items, etc.): the floor will be empty.
** Therefore, make sure not to leave behind something that you might want to use after this floor. The strategy consisting of teleporting outside of Mom and Mom's Heart to retrieve something that was left behind after fighting them is '''not''' viable here.
** The {{r|Boss Rush}} entrance will disappear if it was previously open.
** If a {{M|Shop Restock Machine}} is used within the now-empty shop, it will restock the shop as normal.
** If the effect of {{i|Forget Me Now}} is invoked after the special version of Mom's Heart is defeated, the {{cu|Darkness}}-like effect will remain on the newly generated floor. Additionally, no items will naturally generate in rooms where they would have. After the player defeats Mom again, there will be no flesh door, and the trapdoor to Corpse will appear.
* The alternative floor to Mausoleum is {{s|Gehenna}}. It is unlocked after all bosses from this floor have been defeated.

